= Strange Companion

Once Weed finished his business in Rosenheim Kingdom, he headed into the Plains of Despair again. This time, he was riding a horse. It was a cheap, common breed, known for its short stature, short and muscular legs, and good endurance.

People who wanted to make an impression, were usually picking a horse of pure black or white color. But Weed certainly wasn’t one of them, so he chose a simple brown one.

“Okay. Let’s go. Come on, run!”

Loudly hitting the ground with its hooves, the horse broke into a gallop. In rocky or swampy areas it wouldn’t be the best means of transportation, but on the plains, across which Weed was traveling, it was unrivaled.

“Yeah. It’s worth the money.”

He was enjoying the fast and comfortable journey. Now Weed could understand why other people bought horses. But he still was bitter about spending the money! So he had to constantly comfort himself about it.

"Making good investments is the only way to success.”

Though he only spent 3 gold on it, he had to constantly justify his new purchase to not feel regret. He was doing everything to suppress his greedy nature.

But whatever his justification, the horse really was a worth investment, as it allowed him to travel a lot faster than even when he was using Quadruped Run skill.

In a single day he reached the border and passed into the Plains of Despair, then he changed direction and started to move in a strange pattern. The plains had passable terrain and great visibility in every direction, but Weed moved unusually: he rode to the south-east for an hour, then made a sharp turn and rode another hour to north-east.

Making such zigzags, he was gradually making his way to the east towards the fortress of Dark Elves, though he had to spend his valuable time on meaningless wandering.

A few hours later Weed encountered the party that was hunting on the Plains again. Oberon and his companions had just finished another fight and were resting. Of course, they were alert and noticed the approaching rider first.

“What in the world...”

“There’re solo players who come here?”

Everyone in Oberon’s party turned around and looked at Weed in surprise.

When they entered the Plains of Despair, they had to fight monsters almost non-stop. In Rosenheim Kingdom they could brag that they could deal with any monster, but here it was different. They’ve got to learn what real battle is the hard way.

Abyss Knights, Lightning Casters, Poison Lords, Dark Dancers, Night Lords! These, and many other monsters of level 350 and above, were setting traps, making ambushes, casting deadly spells and summoning minions to aid them in battle.

These lands were a real challenge for their party. A couple times they had encountered monsters of level 400 or higher, and it was only by their tremendous effort that their hunt didn’t end at that moment. With every day, the mood in the party was getting gloomier and gloomier.

So it was no wonder that, the moment Oberon saw Weed, his eyes took a perfectly round shape.

“Hey, you! It is dangerous here. This is the Plains of Despair... Hurry up, turn around and get away from here as fast as you can! Or no, we better escort you back.”

Oberon was a really noble man. He was ready to defend others even when he was being attacked himself. The warrior profession was often picked by such open, good-mannered, and kind people.

But Weed wasn’t anywhere near that kind of guy. It could be said that he was the exact opposite. Weed just rode past them, totally ignoring the players. But, just like their previous meeting, he didn't ignore the items left by them on the ground!

He didn’t even get off the horse to pick them up, he just bent over to gather them into his saddlebag, holding on the horse only by his legs.

‘I must gather everything.’

Having picked up the items, Weed continued his journey to the east.

“Huh? He just left?”

“Does he not value his life?”

Players from the hunting party were watching him ride away.

“Everyone is free to choose his own way to die.”

“Really, there are people who like to travel alone everywhere.”

However Pluto, Oberon, Hyacinth and a couple other veterans weren’t so quick with conclusions. Weed’s behavior wasn’t that of a person who was going to die in near future.

A few thoughts flashed in Oberon’s mind. He remembered how they encountered Soulless Wolves right after passing the border, and how they'd seen a strange Orc who picked up all the items left after the fight.

“Could it be...”

Pluto looked at Oberon.

“That Orc!”

“So it was a player?”

“If that was a player, then...”

They nodded to each other.

"A player who can turn into an Orc... Only one person comes to mind.”

The others understood now what Oberon was implying. After all, this hunting party consisted of high level players very passionate about Royal Road.

“The Hall of Fame!”

“The Orc from that video!”

“He looked different this time, but that’s him! The same terrible face.”

“Right. There are no Orcs in the game as ugly as this one!”

“So that event is going to happen in the Plains of Despair!”

@<embed>{|html|<hr/>}

Though this time Weed was traveling on a horse, his mood wasn’t quite as good as it should have been. On his way he had noticed traces of the hunting party, or, to be precise, items, left by them.

Weed could see them clearly, but couldn’t come close enough to pick them up. There were strong monsters living in those areas that would be hard to deal with alone. Besides, the hunting party was coming through the middle of these areas where the number of monsters was the greatest.

At first glance, the plains looked like they were empty, but that was a misleading illusion. Every kind of monster had its own territory, and if a player walked into one of these territories, all of the monsters inhabiting it were forced to attack. These territories were scattered around the plains, forming a complex labyrinth.

Weed had a copy of the map, so he was able to avoid all the dangerous areas. But even with that map and a horse, he had to follow a winding path which really slowed him down.

After a day of constant galloping, the horse started to foam at the corners of its mouth. It was getting exhausted. It was especially bad since Weed was still carrying a pretty weighty Orc statue in one of his bags.

Usually, horse owners took care of their rides: stroking them, comforting them, feeding carrots to them, and of course letting them rest when they were tired.

Weed was rushing his horse instead. “Come on, run. You can do it. You belong to a species of runners after all, and aren't you disappointed that you never actually reached your limit?”

After that, he suddenly started to thump out a tempo on the horse’s back. And it did start running a bit faster, expending the little power it still had. But after some time the speed started to drop again.

“It’s hard, isn’t it? Hold on a bit more. When we arrive you’ll be able to rest as much as you want.”

The horse believed those words, and put some more effort into it, stabilizing their speed.

Weed’s kind voice and his high Charisma and Leadership stats were helping him to convince the poor horse to run ahead in hopes of reaching their destination.

But however long it ran, there was no sign of their destination and Weed wasn’t letting it slow down.

“Come on, a little further.”

The horse was running.

“Almost there.”

It was still believing.

“Just a bit left.”

Weed’s behavior towards his mount went beyond horrible. He was squeezing every last drop from the horse.

In the end it couldn’t stand such treatment any longer, and made a last few steps before falling to the ground completely exhausted.

After examining the heavily breathing horse and realizing that he wouldn't be able to ride it any further, Weed took his bags off it and said, “You’re free now. Go wherever you want. Good luck.”

He took out the small Orc statue. He didn’t have time to wait for the horse to recover, so he switched to his original way of traveling.

“Sculpture Transformation!”

The journey to Rosenheim Kingdom had taken him seven days. But now that he covered a significant part of the way on the horse and saved his strength, he figured he'd be able to make it back in half that time.

“Chwiik! Chwik!”

The small Orc headed to the east.

He still was terribly short on time. He'd previously visited all the villages of the exiles in the center of the plains, but now he had to visit as many of the remote ones as possible.

Factoring that into his route back to the fortress, it was going to take about 12 days.

“And I have 15 days until the battle starts.”

Having concluded that he had just enough time, Weed continued to run when all of a sudden, he noticed someone standing on a hill. The person was standing with their back to Weed and looking at something out of Weed’s field of view.

“A player? How... It’s not easy to get here. That must be some villager. Chwiit!”

Villages of exiles were scattered all around the plains. And despite the abundance of monsters, they were full of life: villagers were hunting and traveling to other villages for other business. It was not unusual to meet one of them here.

“Chwiik, is there a village nearby?”

As he came closer, he noticed more details about the person on the hill. Graceful posture, waist-long hair... ‘It must be a woman.’

Though he could only see her back, his sculptor’s senses were telling him, that she must be very beautiful. A woman watching the sunset. No, a young lady.

Deciding that it was not his business, Weed continued to run. The girl could obviously hear him, but wasn’t paying him any attention, so he decided to simply run past her.

While running up the hill, Weed noticed something at the edge of his field of view. A huge bull-like monster was running in the same direction.

“Plains Hunter!”

That was one of the few kinds of monsters that didn’t live on some set territory. Plains Hunters roamed all over the Plains of Despair, hunting people and even, occasionally, monsters.

Villagers said that they were around level 320, and were formed when warriors got cursed by a dark spell and turned into monsters with large health pool and an unpleasant ability to reduce a player’s max health a bit with every hit.

That last feature made them incredibly hard to fight against.

Weed prepared for a hard battle. “Damn. I didn’t even sharpen my sword or polish my armor...”

He was focused on running, so he didn’t prepare for a fight at all. And the difference between fighting after preparations and fighting unprepared was huge.

If he had encountered the monster on plain terrain, he’d be able to go around the monster. But on a slope, he noticed it too late and there was no way to avoid a fight.

However, the Plains Hunter wasn’t going for Weed, but for the girl standing on the top of the hill! He saw it begin to stalk towards her.

‘Great. I’ll escape in the meanwhile... Oh, no, I can’t run away!’

At first Weed got relieved and was going to use the opportunity to escape, but then he remembered another trait of that kind of monster. Plains Hunters always chased their prey to the end.

Once it finished the girl, it’d follow Weed until it caught up with him. And that would most probably happen when Weed was tired after running for days, which would make fighting with it even harder.

So, his best bet would be to deal with it now. Besides this monster had a certain weak point.

‘While it’s busy with the girl, I’ll come from behind and stab it.’

The Hunter aimed his spear at the girl.

Weed got a better grip on his glaive. He was counting on making a single powerful strike that would most likely be lethal.

He thought he planned for every possibility. But in the last moment, the girl turned around with incredible speed and unsheathed her sword! The blade flashed and seemingly split into 3 separate edges, which immediately struck the Hunter that was about to thrust his spear forward.

The next moment, the monster was dead.

The girl looked at Weed. When their eyes met, Weed was stunned.

He knew her. Knew her well!

That was Seoyoon.

“Chwi, chwiik...”

He froze with a glaive lifted in a striking position. If anyone had been watching, it looked like an ugly small Orc was about to attack a lone girl.

@<embed>{|html|<hr/>}

After leaving the Rosenheim Kingdom, Seoyoon went on a long journey before reaching the Plains of Despair.

Her class was Berserker, which allowed her to master all kinds of weapons. However, her real power showed when fights dragged on for a long time. Instead of getting tired like a normal player, the Berserker profession allowed her to recover her stamina and even get stronger over time as long as she kept killing enemies.

Seoyoon fought like a machine, as any real Berserker should. No matter day or night, she was restlessly hunting and slaying one monster after another, leaving only dead bodies behind.

Sometimes, during her journey, she would get stranded in the center of some dungeon and die as a result. Even a player like her, who had been fighting non-stop since the launch of Royal Road, couldn’t win against such an overwhelming number of opponents.

In many ways, death didn't bother her too much: levels and skill proficiency weren't too important to her as she preferred fighting monsters with her own movements rather than bothering with skills.

However, she wasn’t able to play for 24 hours after death, so she still tried not to die. Her goal was to win every fight.

Though, killing monsters and clearing dungeons wasn’t her actual goal either. She only needed battles to let out the accumulated frustration! To take revenge! And monsters wouldn’t find even a spark of compassion in her cold eyes.

Seoyoon noticed the Orc that was approaching her with glaive in hand and looked straight at him. ‘Enemy,’ she thought.

She didn’t relax for a single moment, as a new fight could start any moment now. The sword in her hand turned towards a new target.

@<embed>{|html|<hr/>}

Seoyoon.

Having recognized her, Weed froze in place.

Beautiful. He had already seen her before, but now that he met her again he couldn’t avert his gaze, her beauty struck him too hard.

‘A human can’t be this beautiful...’

It seemed like her face was shining. Her eyes, mouth, nose - everything was in harmony, filling her face with incredible charm.

After seeing Seoyoon so close, Weed felt despair. He had created so many sculptures, but none of them reflected her beauty properly.

If it was possible, he’d look at her like this all day. He would never get tired of it. But right now wasn’t the best time for that. He had to get away from here, before something terrible happened.

If he was discovered to be the player who created a sculpture of her without permission, he thought, he might end up like the Plains Hunter.

However strong Weed considered himself, Seoyoon had a pretty high level even at their first meeting. And all the items she was wearing were above level 300!

‘Trouble.’

Besides, the situation was very delicate. An Orc with a glaive was assaulting a lone girl.

Weed swallowed. Of course, he thought, he'd just explain it to her and clear the situation.

“Chwi, Chwiik!”

Weed was hurried and agitated, so all that came out of his mouth were meaningless orcish sounds!

“Chwichik...”

“Chwi-i-i-it!”

Every time he tried to say something, he ended up just spitting in Seoyoon’s direction instead!

Then, he felt a sinister aura coming out of Seoyoon’s body. Like she was already slicing him in pieces in her mind. It was making his body go numb and his knees tremble. It was menacing and oppressing... the breath of death!

That overwhelming pressure made Weed think that he’d die even if he explained himself. But he had to at least try. He must tell her that he’s that guy she once shared a meal with in the instructor’s house.

Though... even that fact might not stop her, he thought. Even the most beautiful rose has thorns. After all she already had a red mark of player-killer on their first meeting.

She was the first Player-Killer Weed had met in Royal Road.

‘Who would think that in Plains of Despair I would meet the person I never expected to meet again.’

Since that memorable meeting at the instructor's dinner table, the image of that beautiful but cold girl was imprinted in his memory. Every time Weed created a new sculpture, he tried to give her face different expressions in his imagination. He tried to fill this cold angel with a living beauty.

“Chwiik!”

Weed opened his eyes wide and looked forcefully at Seoyoon.

If his opponent was a murderer, the fact that he was a player too might only encourage her to attack. But it might prevent her from attacking as well.

‘Can I defeat her?’

Even if he were to give it his all, he was still significantly behind her in levels and equipment quality. At first sight, judging by her items, he was behind by about 70 levels.

‘A few months ago Bard Ray had level 370. Now he should be around 390. Though her level is slightly lower, she was still among the top players!’

Weed wasn’t afraid of players with higher level than his. He compensated with the difference using his crafting skills, heightened stats, and Sculpting!

But for him, who had started to play to earn money, the worst enemies were Player Killers. They were bandits.

While ordinary players like Weed participate in hard quests and battles to acquire items, these murderers train to fight against players. In the end, they kill other players and take their items!

Though he'd already encountered and defeated the player-killing Dwichigi Quartet, that case was very different. Seoyoon was going to be a tough opponent.

She had gone through the same training in the training hall that he did, so he couldn’t rely on higher stats. And he hadn't been able to use some of his other buff skills like sword sharpening and armor polishing. Besides, a fighting profession like hers must have some unknown to him skills too.

He didn’t see any way out!

However, Weed put even more intensity into his glare. He had to radiate the opposite of how he felt inside: That he’s at least the same strength as her, if not stronger! And then, he could use that chance to get away!

Weed already prepared 36 different escape scenarios.

But then Seoyoon simply lowered her sword, turned around, and continued on her way.

Weed couldn’t understand what just happened. In his eyes, she must not have seen any threat, so she didn’t do anything to him. What he didn't know was that Seoyoon only fought monsters that attacked her first!

The confused Weed quickly came to his senses. ‘Anyway, I don’t have time for this.’

He continued to run towards the Yuroki Mountains.

But Seoyoon started moving too. And, surprisingly, they were going in the same general direction. Therefore, a few days later, their paths crossed again.

At first Weed couldn’t understand how that could have happened. He was running as fast as he could for two days straight, and yet Seoyoon was slightly ahead of him.

But then he realized: He had to avoid all the monsters and their territories while visiting the exiles' villages at the same time. Of course his path was much longer and more difficult. Unlike him, Seoyoon was walking straight, fighting all the monsters on her way!

“Chwi, chwiik!”

Weed was hurt. He was putting all his effort into running, but they still were moving with an equal speed! And Seoyoon was simultaneously hunting monsters and receiving experience and items.

The third time, they met shortly before a place labeled Yunopu Canyon on his map. This canyon was a rocky pass between two large mountains in the northern Plains of Despair. The geography funneled travelers through the canyon -- the only other way to get to the other side would be to go around the mountains or climb over, which would not be easy.

“I don’t have much time, chwiik!” Weed decided to go through the Yunopu Canyon.

So, they traveled together for a while. He was a bit worried about having to follow Seoyoon, so he decided to keep some distance from her to avoid danger -- both from the monsters she was attacking, and from her. But Seoyoon wasn’t paying any attention to the Orc that was following her, she was just making her own her way.

This area was inhabited by giant Yetis. They were around level 340, and had thick white fur that made them immune to ice magic.

They used to live in the mountains, but were driven out by other even more powerful monsters, so they moved into the canyon as it was a popular route for hunters in the Plains of Despair.

“Can’t help it! I will have to fight with the Yetis.”

As she entered the canyon, Weed watched Seoyoon demonstrate her outstanding sword mastery on the first Yetis.

“She’s strong...”

While running through Plains of Despair, Weed had avoided most of the monsters, but in Yunopu Canyon he had to fight Yetis head-on.

Even with his crafting skills, every fight required all of his skill. During fights his health often dropped to critical levels, but for now Weed was winning them.

In contrast, it seemed that fighting didn’t require any effort for Seoyoon. Using her techniques, with incredible grace she was killing several Yetis at a time.

Of course she had a higher level and better equipment, but Weed noticed something else: Skill.

Royal Road was a game set in virtual reality. Here, no matter how high the level of one's skills and abilities, only by using one's movement skills and combat sense effectively was one able to realize the full potential of their profession.

To demonstrate, consider a duel between a monk and a swordsman, two of the professions most popular among players. The player with a sword would try to keep his opponent at a certain distance during the duel, while the monk, on the other hand, would try to approach as closely as possible.

If their skills were at an equal level, the outcome of the duel would depend on their tactics, reaction times, and a bit of luck. And in this case, the fighter with the most experience and skill would most likely win.

Of course, that wasn’t as important during monster hunts, though newbies who didn’t want to learn at all could be killed even by the weakest monsters.

However, even experienced fighters didn’t have a chance against Weed, who had spent an entire year in the real world learning swordsmanship.

‘Nice moves.’

Weed was admiring Seoyoon’s sword skill. Her technique wasn’t as organized as his own. Weed’s swordsmanship didn’t have any weaknesses. He was correctly using all his muscles, concentrating his strength on defense or sudden offense.

Sometimes Weed got carried away and rushed into battle, completely forgetting about defense. He relied primarily on his agility and reaction time, and would rain strikes on his enemies, defeating them sooner or later.

But Seoyoon fought in a different manner. She was thinking about defense and offense at the same time. When she saw a weakness, she would attack. When she was in danger, she would defend.

Of course, she had clearly developed these tactics through countless fights against AI-controlled monsters, not people, which was why her skill would eventually reach a limit. But Weed envied her anyway. In the battle, she would rely on her high agility to fluidly weave around monsters and hit them where they weren't expecting -- In a way, she looked like she was dancing. It was a very... feminine way of fighting, he thought.

When the situation allowed it, Weed watched the girl’s actions with his full attention.

‘She likes to hunt!’

During this entire time, she hadn't said a single word and was always fighting with the same cold expression. It gave the impression that these terrifying monsters weren't even a challenge for her.

But Weed saw something else. Deep inside her beautiful, cold face was hidden sadness. Some burden on her heart.

Ever since their first meeting, Weed often had thought about her inner world. He didn’t have much experience in understanding people and reading faces back then and didn’t see much other than her cold expression.

Now he could understand people’s feelings better and was able to see a bit deeper.

‘Why is she so sad?’ Weed tried to take even closer look at her.

Though he was captivated by her secret, just watching her was no less pleasant. He had never before seen a girl of such beauty that he couldn’t capture in a sculpture, no matter how many times he tried.

While watching her, Weed noticed something else.

Seoyoon never aimed at the opponent’s head. Though Yetis were more than 2 meters tall (~6"6') and the girl was about 1.67 meter (~5"5), with her sword she would be able to hit it anyway.

Weed would definitely aim for the head, as it was the least protected part and hitting it would likely be a critical strike.

But Seoyoon never went for the face. It looked like she wasn’t even looking at their faces. She was just using all the techniques available to her to kill her opponents as fast as possible.

‘She doesn’t look at their expressions? Maybe she’s afraid to see their pain... No, there’s most likely some other reason.’

Because Weed was following Seoyoon, he didn’t have to fight much. He was mostly fighting the few enemies who tried to attack the girl from behind.

“Chwiik, experience!”

Yeti hides were a top grade tailoring material and were worth a lot. Besides the resistances it provided, their fur looked very impressive and clothes made from it were very warm.

“Chwichichichit!”

‘If I pick it all up, I can forget about cold. I’ll sew clothes and even earn some extra money.’

Weed got absorbed into hunting and gathering hides.

“...”

Seoyoon continued to fight and paid no attention to her unexpected companion. But every time she turned around now, she always saw a small Orc behind her.

She still didn’t say a word, and Weed considered it natural. He didn’t hear her talk before as well. Besides even ordinary players wouldn’t talk to him now that he was transformed into Karichwi.

Though at first he was worried a bit about following her, Weed eventually realized that she wouldn't attack him. It became clear after he watched her for some time and saw that she was trying to avoid fighting Yetis who had young.

‘How did she became a murderer? And if she is a kind person inside, she doesn’t have to walk around with such a cold expression then.’

Weed was very curious, but as he didn’t like others intruding on his personal life, he was trying not to intrude into hers. So, the only thing left for him was hunting and gathering loot while the pair traveled through Yunopu Canyon. The canyon didn’t have any turns or crossroads or other paths, only one straight and very long road. And it would take four more days to pass it according to the map.

Half a day later, Seoyoon made a stop to rest. She took out some stale barley bread, which she had stocked up on back at Rosenheim Kingdom, and started to chew it slowly.

Weed respected Seoyoon for that.

“Yeah, to reduce expenses one should start with the food. If you do that, you can accumulate lots of money. Money is power. One should constantly save up, then you will never run out.”

But unlike the girl, Weed wasn’t eating only barley bread. Because of his high cooking skill, he was able to gather ingredients during the hunt and then, with a bit of spices, cook himself tasty and almost free meals. These didn’t only satisfy his hunger, but also boosted his stats.

Weed lit a fire, threaded Yeti meat on wooden sticks, and started to slowly roast it over the flames. The tasty aroma of roasted meat gradually spread around him.

“Chwiik!”

When it was ready, Weed grabbed one of the skewers with both hands and started to eat. The thin Orc was eating with great appetite.

//table{
--------------
Your Satiety increases.
 * Stamina increased by 40%
 * Health increased by 15%
You ate the flesh of Yeti, a monster with great strength.
As a result your strength has been slightly increased for a certain period.
//}

Intermediate cooking skill!

Some people relied on fixed recipes that called for precise timing and exact amounts of ingredients. But Weed had achieved everything through practice cooking great numbers of meals for the parties he used to command.

So even the most simple dishes, when cooked by Weed, were very tasty. Besides, they slightly increased stats.

“...”

While eating, Weed glanced at Seoyoon. He thought that she’d continue walking after eating the bread and he’d have to catch up with her. After all, in a canyon filled with Yetis, even the most intimidating companion was important.

However, to his great surprise, the girl was standing just a few steps away, staring at the Orc. Or, to be precise, at the meat in his hands. The tasty-smelling roasted yeti meat!

“Chwiik!”

Weed was stunned for a moment, but then quickly handed her the other meat stick. He could hunt for meat and cut another stick from a free branch, all of it was certainly not worth risking his life.

Since that moment, Seoyoon always joined the small Orc for meals. In this journey Weed, completely unexpectedly, became her personal chef.

Though he didn’t think it was quite fair. ‘If I don’t share, she might eat me... She’s a murderer after all.’
